You could have something like:
damage = (hp<=25)? 25 : hp-rn2(25)-1
to get pretty much the same effect. One hit nearly kills you (or kills
if weak), and a follow-up hit will definitely kill.

Or: if you have half disintegration resistance then a hit does minimal
damage, and removes the intrinsic.

Or you could do something with Constitution damage.

Almost anything would be better than 50% of maxhp, which creates a
weird instadeath discontinuity at maxhp/2 and confuses the way hit
points are used to measure survivability and danger.

